1
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,497
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,040
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,800
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,457
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting.

11
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,397
Either way, I'm feeling alive!

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,837
Look out below.

13
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:37,080
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,397
Raise your flag up high.

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,040
Hail a brand new dawn.

16
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,837
Blaze across the sky.

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,837
Time to journey on.

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,317
On your mark.

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,217
Camel of other things.

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,137
We're on Earth, a legendary.

21
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,050
Hooray!

22
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:57,600
If you can show your breath,
Then we'll make some waves.

23
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:00,377
We run our daunted.

24
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,617
Ain't no beginners.

25
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,357
Cause if you're wanted,
Then you're a winner.

26
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,840
For we are on the cruise,
And freedom is the only rule.

27
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:12,277
Fearless night and day.

28
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,160
Cause that's just our way.

29
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,197
Find one piece.

30
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,537
I'll be the first.

31
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,817
I've heard it be so fast.

32
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:20,730
I could burst.

33
00:01:20,813 --> 00:01:22,137
It's all this real.

34
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,340
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel.

35
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,437
I'm done playing, filled with the waiting.

36
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:33,137
In a world I'm feeling
alive, but I'll be loud.

37
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:37,040
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

38
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far.

39
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,320
Gotta make it to the end.

40
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,677
Whatever danger we find,
no one ever left behind.

41
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,780
I've always got your back, my friend.

42
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward.

43
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,117
Dreaming from the very
first day I'd make my name.

44
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,220
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed.

45
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave.

46
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,277
In every world I'm feeling alive.

47
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,577
Look out below.

48
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:13,000
Wake up, sunshine.

49
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:17,140
Wake up, sunshine.

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,240
Wake up, sunshine.

51
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:33,987
Meanwhile, at Candy Factory Town,
in the center of the island.

52
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:36,250
Bostama?

53
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,460
Hey, are you okay?

54
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:41,057
He's chewing right
through the factory walls.

55
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,669
Yeah, like he was nothing.

56
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,400
My fangs eat for long.

57
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:04,920
What's this crap?

58
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,937
I don't want some trendy cappuccino latte

59
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,157
thing or fancy sponge
cake when I'm hungry.

60
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,617
That junk's not real food.

61
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,582
What in the hell do I look like?

62
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,740
I'm sorry, boss.

63
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,017
I'll get something else.

64
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,817
That's good, because you're starting
to look pretty tasty yourself.

65
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,857
For a snack, I like fish
bones, and I like them big.

66
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:21,770
Now, go!

67
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,800
Oh, sure thing. Big fish bones. I got it.

68
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:26,740
Never mind.

69
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:31,577
I'm going to go whimp my appetite on some
soldiers and maybe the Ryo family, too.

70
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:34,895
Guess I'll see the rest of
you bums at Conchcord Plaza.

71
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,397
Don't you dare be late.

72
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,892
We all have to be there.

73
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:40,800
What should we do about
the citizens? Come on.

74
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,097
Did you morons pay attention
to a word Captain Horde said?

75
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,900
He told us, no more
stepping on her picture.

76
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,960
Leave him alone for now.

77
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,977
Those losers will get what's
coming to them soon enough.

78
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:53,890
Yeah, yeah.

79
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,786
How are we supposed to
stand up to these guys?

80
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:15,197
Including Heart, the new Fishman pirates
have Horshark Fishman as officers.

81
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,940
And a giant squidfishman.

82
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,717
Not to mention their bodyguard
is a blue-ringed octopus

83
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:24,077
merman known as the best
swordsman on the entire island.

84
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:28,340
I think the Neptune brothers are
the only hope we've got left.

85
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:32,220
Then all we can do is keep the faith.

86
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,860
At Waterwheel Town in the
island's northern region.

87
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:38,450
Did you hear?

88
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:40,897
The princes are making
their way to Concord Plaza.

89
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,745
This country's in such a mess.

90
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,857
Tell me about it.

91
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,717
All we wanted to do was improve
our relationship with the humans.

92
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:50,317
There's no reason to threaten everyone
with death like some kind of madman.

93
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:53,617
And on top of those threats,
they want to execute the king.

94
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:56,157
Maybe Heart will be
willing to bargain with us.

95
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,711
After all, we've got his men held hostage.

96
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,840
Your plan isn't going to work.

97
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:04,277
Boss Heart would rather you
cut us Downson than negotiate.

98
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:07,077
He's more ruthless than
the other fishman pirates.

99
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,866
That's why he looks
Downson on the rest of us.

100
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,680
This can't be good.

101
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:15,037
Ever since the prince has defeated him,

102
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,657
Officer Dosan's power level
has dropped to Downson.

103
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:19,477
Now he's just weak and gloomy.

104
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,560
Let me give him an energy steroid.

105
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:26,440
Thinking about it just brings
me Downson. It's depressing.

106
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:37,137
Heart doesn't like fishmen who
do business with human pirates.

107
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:39,632
He'll give them the Bumson without mercy.

108
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:41,210
Bumson?

109
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:45,900
All those fishmen who donated their
blood to help out wounded humans?

110
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:50,340
He gave them the old Whompson
in the dark of night. Whompson?

111
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:54,378
Hardy believes that human
blood is naturally tainted.

112
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:58,060
And whenever we receive their
blood or offer them our own,

113
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:00,960
we dose in our pure blood under service!

114
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,760
He's back to saying docent now.

115
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:08,240
Any fishman who supports humans is
a traitor and needs to be punished.

116
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:12,747
Our people will never be able
to advance with them in our way.

117
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:14,940
All right, that's enough.

118
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:18,360
I'm gonna go whamson on you!

119
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,029
He's higher than thousand!

120
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,871
The chains are shattered!

121
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,900
You bastard!

122
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,260
They knocked him out with
one swing! Mukabushi!

123
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:37,040
I'll get you back with a slant, son!

124
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:42,420
Then I'll smash your face
with a big, fat boom, son!

125
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:54,300
My enemies will face doom, son!

126
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:58,400
Hit the Cunchcord Plaza for
the execution! Let's move!

127
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:07,156
At the south part of the island, in
front of the Fishman Cultural Hall,

128
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,130
Huh?

129
00:07:11,213 --> 00:07:12,220
Oh, you call it drunk.

130
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,290
Oh, yeah, that's right.

131
00:07:13,373 --> 00:07:14,203
It's me.

132
00:07:14,286 --> 00:07:15,357
This isn't funny anymore, boss!

133
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,617
Pull yourself together.

134
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,537
You're in no shape to fight like that.

135
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:21,340
I think you worry too much, pal. Relax.

136
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,677
Drinks are on the house.

137
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,590
It's my treat.

138
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,517
That's not important right now.

139
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:28,357
Fukaboshi is leading
Neptune's army into the plaza.

140
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,057
We have to be ready for them.

141
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:33,964
Even worse, if things go bad,
Jinbei might even show up to fight.

142
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,840
This isn't a joke, boss!

143
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,540
It's no use!

144
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,577
He's weak as a sea cucumber
and just as slippery!

145
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:42,490
Huh?

146
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,400
How about me?

147
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:47,637
How'd you get your head
spinning around like that?

148
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,132
Ugh, I'm standing still!

149
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,300
How drunk are you? This is awful!

150
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,696
I doubt Yasuie can even hold his sword!

151
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,460
Sure I can.

152
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:57,897
Get away from him immediately!

153
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:58,810
I'm serious!

154
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:02,717
Yasuie will slice into anyone and
everyone when he's this drunk!

155
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,937
Make a run for it!

156
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:06,060
You slice anyone.

157
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:15,000
He attacked his own guys.

158
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,420
See, I can fight just fine.

159
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,940
Right, boys!

160
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:54,117
Hey, Yasuie, why don't
you go to the plaza?

161
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,717
There you can cut up the royal
family as much as you want.

162
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:57,630
Huh?

163
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:01,860
I, uh, know why, uh, nah What?

164
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,097
What is that even supposed to mean?

165
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:07,651
At the marine shopping mall in
the east part of the island?

166
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:13,851
You think you pathetic civilian stand
a chance you're dumber than I thought!

167
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,877
Beach can blend in perfectly with the
surroundings to camouflage himself.

168
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:22,520
Just like a chameleon
He might be on our side,

169
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:25,522
but even we have trouble
figuring out where he is

170
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:30,417
What this is unfair how are we supposed
to fight someone we can't even see?

171
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:34,794
You might as well start begging for
the Neptune brothers to bail you out?

172
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,360
Without them you're finished!

173
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:41,500
Though frankly don't expect
them to last long either.

174
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:44,140
Oh well time to finish you

175
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,357
Did we get it is it dead?

176
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,640
Yeah, we got it

177
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:09,737
You fools have nowhere to run it's only a

178
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,977
matter of time before
we hunt you all down?

179
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:15,497
There's no escaping our
wrath he's talking like

180
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,717
nothing happened we
just beat him to a boat!

181
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:21,741
What class no wonder he's called
the noble of the fishman district?

182
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,100
Prepare for the revolution.

183
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,600
Later on today, at Conchcord Plaza.

184
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:34,600
The Neptune family will die,
and a new king will rise.

185
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,360
Now, let's head to the execution.

186
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:42,166
How much longer before
we arrive at the plaza?

187
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,860
Less than an hour, sir!

188
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:48,017
Executing the king at Conchcord
Plaza feels calculated.

189
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,977
Why not just do it at the palace?

190
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:53,457
I think Heart might be trying
to lure you princes into a trap.

191
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,320
That is no concern to me.

192
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,506
I look forward to this fight.

193
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,895
I will not let them murder our father.

194
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:01,961
And I refuse to let our citizens'

195
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:05,117
hearts and minds become closed
off after all we've worked for.

196
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,377
Jinbei kept Heart under his watchful eye,

197
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:10,177
and now I see that we should
have taken note of that.

198
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:13,597
He's probably the reason human pirates
have stopped coming here as well,

199
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,817
an issue we should have
investigated sooner.

200
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:18,517
Sandy, do you think Shirahoshi
is still in the hardshell tower?

201
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,957
We haven't heard anything
about Sis in a while,

202
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,569
and it's really starting
to bug Mayfassola!

203
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,877
How did you feel about the Straw Hats?

204
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,037
Because I didn't think
they were bad people.

205
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,337
Madam Charlie said that
they destroyed the country,

206
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,420
but so far they seem like
the least of our worries.

207
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:38,079
They have caused their share of
trouble, but they may be victims too.

208
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:39,837
That's what I think.

209
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:44,391
Straw Hats G-Mae's friend, and the
mermaids didn't have a problem with them.

210
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:47,200
And frankly, their
judgment is really wrong.

211
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:51,817
Agreed, but this is not the time nor
the place to ponder such questions.

212
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:52,730
Right!

213
00:11:52,813 --> 00:11:54,240
We need to focus, Solatido!

214
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,637
Summon every soldier that
the country has to offer!

215
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:00,880
We're going to save our
king at any cost! Yes, sir!

216
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:05,640
At Fishfilly Hills in the
northeast part of the island...

217
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,600
It's too tough! Damn it,

218
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:12,417
we shouldn't be having this much trouble
fighting against just one sea monster!

219
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:15,400
But then again, it seems
something is amiss!

220
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:21,152
The energy steroids are making him crazy!

221
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:24,140
Hey, calm down, sea bear. That's enough.

222
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,217
The soldiers are barely alive.

223
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,535
Our job here is done.

224
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:28,890
Use this.

225
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,500
Sea kings don't like fire. Stay back!

226
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:52,397
What the I don't think his arms are
supposed to bend back like that.

227
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:57,217
He must be under some kind of a curse
you idiot put out that fire right away!

228
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,130
Sakehi!

229
00:12:58,213 --> 00:12:59,420
Hot, hot, hot! Huh?

230
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:02,260
He said something about fire? Fire!

231
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:04,677
What are you trying to do?

232
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:06,137
Cook up some smoked squid?

233
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,517
You think we'd eat you?

234
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,440
Oh, the fire.

235
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:13,557
You were trying to roast me and
have me with a glass of sake, he.

236
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:15,405
When I recover, I'll kill you.

237
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,637
Who'd want to do that?

238
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,550
You're crazy!

239
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:18,800
Oh, sorry, sir.

240
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,390
Careful.

241
00:13:20,473 --> 00:13:24,025
I heard about how one of Ikoros'
best friends was a giant squid.

242
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:26,257
One day, he swam too close to the sun.

243
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:29,105
Before you know it, he
was a giant dried squid.

244
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:31,985
That's why Icarus freaks
out when he sees fire.

245
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:34,740
I'm sorry, Dinolos!

246
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,737
But if he's a fish man, he doesn't
have anything to worry about.

247
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:40,650
Dinol!

248
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:51,200
No more fire! Got me here! Oh no!

249
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,257
That dried squid spear is dangerous.

250
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:58,157
It turns back into a normal squid by sucking
all the fluid out of anyone it strikes.

251
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,980
That guy's as good as jerky.

252
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,110
Icarus.

253
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:10,500
Wow, that's rough.

254
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,997
First he got dried out
and then this happened?

255
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,597
Okay, boss Icarus, I
think he's had enough.

256
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,117
Isn't it about time we start
making our way to Conchcord Plaza?

257
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,030
We're here.

258
00:14:20,113 --> 00:14:20,943
You're right.

259
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:24,040
It's too late for that
guy. Leave him here.

260
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:25,410
Minister!

261
00:14:25,493 --> 00:14:26,989
You need to see this, sir!

262
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:31,490
Heart!

263
00:14:31,573 --> 00:14:32,840
Is that him up there?

264
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,477
I don't see Heart, but I do see
other men from the Fishman District!

265
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:39,197
They must be heading
for the Conchcord Plaza!

266
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,456
Damn those bastards!

267
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,710
No way!

268
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,657
They still have King Neptune hostage!

269
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,387
You can't let them beat you!

270
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,380
Please do something!

271
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:49,770
Great night!

272
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,200
You people need you!

273
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:54,520
I'm no great knight. Not anymore.

274
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,100
Look at me.

275
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:59,020
I can't even save my poor citizens.

276
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,600
Please hang in there.

277
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:06,240
What good is a king's army if it
can't even protect the king it serves?

278
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,874
We're an embarrassment to this country.

279
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:12,304
Siricaros, just two hours
left to the execution.

280
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:14,760
Come with us to Conchcord Plaza.

281
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,824
What happened to Captain Heart?

282
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,140
Is he not with you?

283
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,860
Why isn't he talking to me directly here?

284
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,960
How about that?

285
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:32,140
That drug enhances your strength
at the cost of your lifespan.

286
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,345
You shouldn't have taken
it in the first place.

287
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:36,880
Shut up.

288
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,560
Captain Heart was injured.

289
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:43,857
The human pirate swordsman cut him
in the gashes too painful to bear.

290
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:44,770
Injured?

291
00:15:44,853 --> 00:15:45,977
The captain got injured?

292
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,777
His body wouldn't stop hurting,

293
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:51,154
so he kept taking energy
steroids to help kill the pain.

294
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,140
Now he's messed up.

295
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,496
We told him to stop, but he
wouldn't listen to anyone.

296
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:02,860
Oh, Captain Head!

297
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,180
I can't breathe.

298
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,657
I can't...

299
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:10,780
I feel like I'm gonna explode.

300
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:13,700
It's just as I suspected.

301
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,162
The drug side effects are
bad enough to kill you.

302
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:31,357
What's wrong with you now, Sea Bear?

303
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,897
I think he must be afraid.

304
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:34,617
But all these Sea Monsters have been under

305
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:37,465
Captain Forty's control
for a really long time.

306
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:40,151
I don't know what would spook him so much.

307
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:03,380
Come on, Captain.

308
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,621
Quit blubbering.

309
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,897
Yeah, things will start looking up soon.

310
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,457
Just get back in the game.

311
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:12,197
Like I would ever take advice
from a couple of losers like you.

312
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:15,637
You guys have no idea what it's
like having your heart broken.

313
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,200
These feelings are real.

314
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:20,640
I've wanted her since
I first saw her. Sure,

315
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:22,180
she was just a kid,

316
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:26,420
but I knew if I married her, I
could fulfill my ancestor's dream.

317
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:29,060
But what happened instead?

318
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,400
You're just not my type! No!

319
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,317
Not my type, she said.

320
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:52,160
When the words came to my
ears, I felt my love grow.

321
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,895
A flawless haiku by Vandertick
in the night, I suspect!

322
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,200
My soul?

323
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,040
It's aching!

324
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:08,209
After she rejected me, I felt like it
was time for a change, so I cut my hair

325
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:10,500
I just attacked!

326
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:13,417
I thought I'd kill her instead,
but I can't even get that right.

327
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:16,757
I know she's alive because I
can still throw things at her!

328
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,880
This is not Straw Hat's fault!

329
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:28,300
Wait, that's it?

330
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:35,640
What's so funny? My idea!

331
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:41,660
If I can't end her existence, then
I'll just have to end everyone else's!

332
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:44,640
It's gonna be great!

333
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:45,800
You'll see!

334
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,010
NEPOSAL

335
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,270
No!

336
00:19:03,353 --> 00:19:04,780
Neptune's Army is done for!

337
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:06,440
Every last one!

338
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:09,940
They didn't stand a chance.

339
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:11,697
The party is too strong.

340
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,980
We are all done for!

341
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:16,040
Minister of the Right!

342
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,075
Minister of the Left!

343
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,800
We couldn't do anything.

344
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,440
We were so close.

345
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,957
You're going to be okay.

346
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:32,300
After so long.

347
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:33,940
Please stay with us.

348
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:38,340
We were finally supposed to see results.

349
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:42,200
This was going to be our
year at the World Summit.

350
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:44,080
Queen Otohime.

351
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:51,497
But then they had to come and ruin
everything someone help us save the

352
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:58,000
king if we don't stop them soon he will
be executed surely someone can fight

353
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:07,317
we can't get in they locked the
entrance to the plaza behind them

354
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:12,400
kingdom tune let's scale the wall
maybe we can see inside Hide!

355
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,460
Thank you.

356
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,080
Let us make haste, Megalo!

357
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:28,608
I thought you soldiers were
supposed to protect this country!

358
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,740
My men!

359
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,320
Damn you, Heart!

360
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,120
Look alive, boys.

361
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,264
That soldier's up to something.

362
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:54,680
You think so?

363
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,840
Looks like he's packing dynamite!

364
00:21:58,020 --> 00:22:01,608
He's gonna blow everyone up with
some kind of suicide attack!

365
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:05,020
But if he does that, I'm
gonna turn into roasted squid!

366
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:09,080
The three princes should get here soon.

367
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:12,956
But I can take out at least
one of you before they do.

368
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:17,500
Oh no, look out!

369
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,160
Water shot.

370
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,080
How far can it go?!

371
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:04,357
You hear that?

372
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,760
That whistling sound! What is it?

373
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:37,100
Oh, my God.

374
00:23:40,100 --> 00:23:41,037
Am I crazy?

375
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:44,708
I was under the impression the
water shot wasn't that strong.

376
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:55,597
I know it took a lot of energy
steroid to get that tough, but still,

377
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:56,797
that was incredible!

378
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:59,037
We never anticipated it changing your hair

379
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:01,597
color or increasing your
muscle mass so greatly,

380
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,510
though.

381
00:24:02,593 --> 00:24:03,886
How are you feeling, Captain?

382
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:05,698
Couldn't be better.

383
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:28,100
What happened here?

384
00:24:29,020 --> 00:24:31,902
Why didn't the soldiers
wait for us to have them?

385
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:48,320
Fukaboshi, Ryoboshi, Mamboshi.

386
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:50,077
Don't underestimate them.

387
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:53,717
Both their ranks and their sea
monsters have been empowered by a drug.

388
00:24:53,800 --> 00:24:54,918
Now it makes sense.

389
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:58,457
On an even playing field, Neptune's
army would never lose a sortie.

390
00:24:58,540 --> 00:24:59,370
No!

391
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,400
It's time to mumble. Ready?

392
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:09,977
Why don't you understand
you're all so pathetic

393
00:25:10,060 --> 00:25:13,377
you new fishman pirates are
just a bunch of cowards!

394
00:25:13,460 --> 00:25:16,117
The other islanders let go of their hurt

395
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:18,237
feelings brought on by
the humans discrimination!

396
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:21,237
And despite the fact that
humans murdered their

397
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:23,977
hero and their queen
they're willing to forgive!

398
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:27,057
Them even after all of
their suffering they still

399
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:30,460
sign their names because
they want to change the?

400
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:33,930
future.

401
00:25:34,013 --> 00:25:35,100
Your highness.

402
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:36,697
Wait for the Beach.

403
00:25:36,780 --> 00:25:39,460
What you do undermines their efforts.

404
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:40,710
Can't

405
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,657
you recognize their bravery?

406
00:25:43,740 --> 00:25:45,297
You're kidding me, right?

407
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:47,840
Don't mistake their kindness for courage.

408
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:51,591
He gives the humans another
excuse to take advantage of us.

409
00:26:15,060 --> 00:26:18,437
you seek revenge not for
justice but because of your

410
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:22,100
own personal hatred I won't
let you take the king's life,

411
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:24,440
nor the island his citizens call home.

412
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:27,400
You will never have the Ryugu kingdom!

413
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:34,780
We're saved!

414
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:38,100
We should have known we
could count on the princes!

415
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:45,860
We will never be defeated, because we've
been granted a power that is absolute.

416
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:52,380
And with that power we will rule this
country the way it was always meant to be.

417
00:26:53,420 --> 00:26:55,697
The future of this country is peace,

418
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:59,017
peace with the humans and peace
with that monsters like you.

419
00:26:59,100 --> 00:27:02,057
If we don't triumph here
we'll have failed and

420
00:27:02,140 --> 00:27:03,777
it will be hundreds of
years before we have.

421
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:06,137
Another shot at friendship
with the human world.

422
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:08,000
Oh is that a fact?

423
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:14,200
Well then the winners of this
fight will rule this country. Ray.

424
00:27:46,100 --> 00:27:48,720
They look... stronger!

425
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:56,940
What? But how?

426
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,840
Too slow.

427
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:36,020
Time is running short, little old.

428
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:38,620
Be safe, Father.

429
00:28:39,100 --> 00:28:40,360
We'll be there soon.

430
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,054
He's going to be fine.

431
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,377
I promise you, Princess.

432
00:28:43,460 --> 00:28:44,420
Thank you.
